          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>On bimanual and rectovaginal examination of a woman with cervical cancer, you fe</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>On bimanual and rectovaginal examination of a woman with cervical cancer, you feel hard, cobblestone-like induration in the tissue lateral to the cervix extending all the way to the pelvic side wall. Which structure is involved?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Parametrium</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Parametrial induration reaching the pelvic side wall indicates local extension beyond the cervix and is a key staging finding on clinical examination.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rectum</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Rectal involvement presents with rectal bleeding or altered bowel habit, and is assessed separately from parametrial induration.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Bladder</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Bladder involvement presents with urinary symptoms such as frequency, dysuria, or haematuria, not parametrial induration.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Vagina</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Vaginal involvement is assessed by direct inspection of the vaginal walls, not by palpating tissue lateral to the cervix.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Hardened, cobblestone tissue lateral to the cervix reaching the pelvic side wall is parametrial involvement — a critical finding that upstages the disease."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct — parametrial induration reaching the pelvic side wall is a hallmark of locally advanced disease."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
